rows.en:
Since then, I still haven't woken from my dream.
And without ever waking from that dream, I'm now living in reality.
Where and how I strayed from the path, I don't know, but the world I'm in now is different somehow.{p}

After the six vanished that day, I just stood there in a daze in front of the old school building.
Once the morning sun had fully shown its face and I could hear the birds singing, people began to appear here and there.
And then the same old everyday life began, unchanged as ever.{p}

That's right.
There's no point sitting at home thinking about it like this.
Holding a faint hope that I might be able to confirm whether what I saw that time was real or a dream, I headed for the school.{p}

And after I got home, I thought it over again.
Maybe people from a world different from ours live in that old school building.
A world completely separate from the one where we live our lives like this.{p}

Come to think of it, I had a mountain of summer homework.
If I didn't do it now, I'd be the one suffering later.
I might as well get at least a little of it out of the way.{p}

No way★
Am I hearing things?
There's no way I could be hearing this voice here.{p}

"Jeez, what a closed-minded guy."
Another voice came from the other side of the room.
This voice...{p}

I glared at them.
"I couldn't have known everyone would vanish! If I'd known, I would have stopped partway!"
In that instant, the smiles vanished from all their faces.{p}

"You're still saying that?"
Iwashita all but spat the words.
"How disappointing. It seems I overestimated you."{p}

...That's it!
I realized what had felt wrong.
Despite the blazing summer sun, there was no shadow at her feet!{p}

...What does she mean?
I picked up a shard of the mirror and looked at my face in it.
What I saw reflected there was...{p}

"Hino★"
The one looking startled on the other side of the mirror was Hino from the newspaper club.
"No way☆"{p}

I hurled the mirror shard to the ground.
I stamped on it again and again.
The shard broke into countless glittering grains.{p}

I slowly raised my head.
The people who had been in the schoolyard were all running toward the old school building.
But I started walking toward the school gate.{p}

A construction worker's deep, booming voice rang out.
I didn't even have time to scream.
I was crushed beneath lumber that came falling from above.{p}

"Hey, {a}. You finally made it.
We've been waiting for you."
Hosoda welcomed me with a beaming smile.{p}

"More to the point, so the Sanzu River really does exist.
I have to say, I'm a little moved."
Arai said it with genuine admiration.{p}

"I'm pretty satisfied myself.
From now on, I get to bully {a} forever.
This is a world where stress doesn't even exist."{p}

"Isn't that the truth.
What a wonderful world this is, where we can bully {a} right out in the open.
Without that, it'd be the worst world imaginable, with nothing in it at all."{p}

I shoved Shindo away and ran.
But it was pointless.
No matter how far I ran, no matter which direction I ran in, I always ended up back with those six.{p}

When I looked closely, I saw that everyone besides Shindo had put on that mask too, at some point.
...I can't escape anymore.
Not from these six, and not from this world...{p}

It was just as I fell into despair.
I heard a voice calling me again.
This time, it was a different voice from before.{p}

An overwhelming despair spread through me.
(What is this?
Is this the last memory of someone who was stabbed to death...?){p}

How many people's images of 'death' had I seen by now?
The bitter regrets of people who, for one reason or another, couldn't pass on went flowing through me.
Each time, a deep despair was left behind inside me.{p}
